From 0910ab6a073b75dda4962d0103fc2cd6890afd2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:32:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(desktop): an unread dot takes its stored
 outcome's tone, not the done emerald
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

desktop.log on the MacBook showed `state=unread ... outcome=waiting` with every
card the chat owned parked: the stripe was the grey waiting glyph, but the dot
painted the emerald `unread` colour, which users read as green / done.

Precedence: the unread dot is emerald only when the stored outcome is `done`
(or absent / an unknown kind, as before). For waiting / running / unresolved /
decision / muted it paints the same colour as that outcome's stripe (grey,
amber, red, grey), still filled so it still reads as new, and its label says
"Unread — <outcome>" instead of "Finished — unread". The unread state itself
(status bucket, unread count, ordering) is unchanged.

Tests: session-outcome.test.ts pins unreadDotOutcomeStripe / label;
session-row.test.tsx renders an unread row with each non-done outcome (and
parked cards) and asserts no emerald, and keeps emerald for done / no outcome.
